also involved in maintaining tolerance to self-antigens, preventing autoimmune diseases. The ability of dendritic cells to bridge the innate and adaptive immune systems makes them critical for effective immunity." checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[104,1409][1176,2072]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="6" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="0.0%" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[211,2234][284,2277]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="7" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="6.2%" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[996,2234][1069,2277]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="8" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="Analysis" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[208,2368][369,2423]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /><node index="9" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.szalongevity.sza_mobile" content-desc="Normal dendritic cell levels indicate a well-balanced immune system capable of effectively detecting and responding to pathogens. Adequate dendritic cell function ensures that the adaptive immune response is properly activated, leading to the production of targeted antibodies and memory cells that provide long-term immunity. Normal levels also help maintain immune tolerance, reducing the risk of autoimmune diseases. Maintaining healthy dendritic cell levels is crucial for overall immune competence and for the body's ability to respond to new infections." checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="true" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[143,2449][1137,2707]" drawing-order="0" hint="" /></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>